<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Matanza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1932">1932</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as 1932 Salvadoran peasant massacre</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Matanza, 'the massacre', was the killing of thousands of peasants, most of them indigenous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pipil">Pipil</a>, by the Salvadoran army and militias after an uprising in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a>-growing west of El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> in January 1932. Estimates of the dead range from about 10,000 to over 30,000. It entrenched military rule under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximiliano-hernandez-martinez">Maximiliano Hernández Martínez</a> and led indigenous communities to hide their identity for generations.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-matanza.jpg" alt="La Matanza" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Netito777, vectorizada por Jarke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapa_levantamiento_campesino_1932.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
